Z||000000||GT Rookie||07-23-2001||12:32 AM||||My GT V6 puffs out a cloud of light bluish gray smoke at startup.  I don't notice it at any other time.  Is there an additive fix or is it just a matter of time before I'll need some work done? ||||reg||9
Z||000001||hyhy4u||07-23-2001||01:01 AM||||There has been a ton of threads on about start up smoke.  It seems to be a something commen to all Fieros and isnt really to much to be concered about..as long as its not smoking permently everything should be ok.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||07-23-2001||01:11 AM||||Its because of leaky valve seals.  They let oil through at start up, but once the engine warms up, they dont leak anymore..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||07-23-2001||10:48 AM||||Nothing to be concerned about.  Even for emissions testing you are aloud up to 5 sec of smoke on start up.  As mentioned above it is the oil from the top of the head leaking down past valve seals-some oil is designed to leak past to lubricate the valve seals-so all vehicles do it to some extent.||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||07-23-2001||03:44 PM||||Here's a new idea! I don't suppose anyone has guessed "valve seals" yet?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Not a terribly difficult job after the first time.  Requires removing the upper plenum, middle intake manifold and valve covers.  Also needed: a valve spring compressor and some downtime.  <P>For me, the thing that takes longest about this job, is cleaning and painting parts, and fixing all the other stuff I find that could use repair and/or "purtying up."||||reg||12
